  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5059",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the regulation of CHP-126 through a series of molecular interactions involving P2X purinoceptors. The drug targets multiple P2X receptors, including P2X1 and P2X7, which are known to mediate cellular signaling through purinergic pathways. These receptors are subsequently targeted by a compound with a known structure, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which is itself a known target of palmarumycin CP18. This compound is a known modulator of P2X receptors and is directly linked to the activation of CHP-126. The evidence suggests a mechanistic pathway where palmarumycin CP18 influences the activity of P2X receptors, which in turn modulate the activity of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, ultimately leading to the activation of CHP-126. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust and well-supported relationship, with the core mechanism involving the modulation of P2X receptors and their downstream effects on CHP-126.",
